    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352">

                <pb facs="0477" n="403" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg403"/>

                <head>Mr. Clay to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 104.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg, Russia</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 28, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir: I</hi> now enclose the comments caused by the
                    Moscow dinner, translated from the Russian press by Secretary Curtin.</p>
                <p>In a few days he will have ready extracts from the journals of the western powers
                    upon the same subject.</p>
                <p>You will judge whether they should be given to the American journals.</p>
                <p>It is believed here that the <hi rendition="#italic">entente cordiale</hi> thus
                    shown between Russia and America will not be without its moral force in your
                    settlement of the Monroe doctrine.</p>
                <p>Very truly, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. M. CLAY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William h. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d352-a1.xml" xpointer="d352-a1"/>
            </div>
